<link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/css/infographic-retail-pos-multi-till.css">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Archivo:wght@600;700&family=Inter:wght@400;500;600&display=swap">
<div class="n3l-retail-pos-multi-till">
<figure class="fig">
  <header class="mast">
    <span class="eyebrow brand-eyebrow">NEXT3LABS &mdash; Retail operations</span>
    <p class="display-title">One till forgives. <span class="hi">Several tills do not.</span></p>
    <p class="sub">Four requirements that only appear once a retail operation runs multiple tills or outlets &mdash; and the question that exposes each one.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="ladder" aria-label="What changes from one till to many">
    <div class="ladder-head" aria-hidden="true">
      <span class="col-label col-label--a">One till</span>
      <span class="col-label col-label--b">Multiple tills &amp; outlets</span>
    </div>
    <div class="row row--stock">
      <div class="row-key">
        <span class="row-no">01</span>
        <h2>Stock</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="cell cell--a">
        <p>A count on one screen. One person notices the drift.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cell cell--b">
        <p>Sync timing, variants, transfers, stocktake locks, adjustment approvals.</p>
        <span class="ask">When does till one learn what till two sold?</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="row row--people">
      <div class="row-key">
        <span class="row-no">02</span>
        <h2>Permissions</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="cell cell--a">
        <p>One login. The owner is standing there anyway.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cell cell--b">
        <p>Rights per person <em>and</em> per till; supervisor approval at the counter; named overrides.</p>
        <span class="ask">Show me this week&rsquo;s overrides.</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="row row--close">
      <div class="row-key">
        <span class="row-no">03</span>
        <h2>End of day</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="cell cell--a">
        <p>Count the drawer. Any gap is in front of you.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cell cell--b">
        <p>Per-till declarations, shift handovers, payment methods split out, variance traced to a till.</p>
        <span class="ask">Which till, which shift, which sale?</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="row row--returns">
      <div class="row-key">
        <span class="row-no">04</span>
        <h2>Returns</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="cell cell--a">
        <p>Reverse the sale. Put the unit back on the shelf.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cell cell--b">
        <p>Bought here, returned there: find the sale, place the stock, book the refund, define the exchange.</p>
        <span class="ask">Whose day carries the refund?</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <figcaption class="foot">
    <span class="eyebrow">Test it on</span>
    <strong>A busy Saturday &middot; two tills open &middot; a shift handover &middot; a cross-outlet return &middot; a close that does not balance</strong>
  </figcaption>
</figure>
</div>
